Overlay patch 0062 (D-081): TOUCH DRAG-LOOK FOR FREE LOOK + TOUCH-C STICK MASK.

A Discord user could not use SoH's Free Look camera (gSettings.FreeLook.Enabled)
with touch controls: the touch overlay has no camera input. the user chose
DRAG-LOOK: a touch that lands on empty overlay space turns the free camera by
finger distance. The shell (app/ios/SohIosShell.m) owns the gesture; this patch
is the game side, three small __IOS__-gated hunks (the desktop build is
byte-for-byte unchanged):

  1. Mouse.cpp -- THE INJECTION POINT. Free Look reads the N64 right stick as a
     RATE (x10 per tick) and then calls Mouse_HandleThirdPerson, which adds the
     mouse delta. Touch drag-look rides exactly that seam: Mouse_UpdatePosRel
     (called once per pad tick from padmgr's Mouse_UpdateAll) drains the
     shell's accumulated drag into a per-tick delta, and Mouse_HandleThirdPerson
     subtracts it the way it subtracts `mouseCoordRel * 40` -- so a drag behaves
     like a mouse move: same sign convention, then SoH's own
     FreeLook.CameraSensitivity.X/Y, FreeLook.InvertXAxis/InvertYAxis and
     MirroredWorld apply on top, unchanged, at every call site
     (SetCameraManual's 15-unit engage threshold, Camera_Free, and the
     door-peek release hook in FreeLook.cpp). NOT gated on EnableMouse: the
     shell only accumulates while Free Look is on and gameplay is live.
     Drained per TICK, not per call: SetCameraManual and Camera_Free both read
     it in the same tick and must agree.

     The trap this avoids: the SDL right-stick axes. LUS's default mapping
     (ControllerDefaultMappings.cpp) binds SDL RIGHTX/RIGHTY to BOTH the
     C-buttons and the N64 right stick, so driving drag-look through them would
     fire C items.

  2. padmgr.c -- THE SAME TRAP, ALREADY SPRUNG BY THE TOUCH C-BUTTONS. They
     emit through SDL RIGHTX/RIGHTY (that is how they reach the C bits), so
     with Free Look on every touch C press also deflected the N64 right stick
     fully and swung the camera for as long as it was held (confirmed on the
     sim, D-081). PadMgr_ProcessInputs now zeroes port 1's right stick while
     SohIos_TouchCMaskActive() -- set by the shell while any touch C is held
     and for 0.25 s after (the virtual axis' release lands on the next SDL
     event pump). The C BITS are untouched, so items/ocarina still work.
     Physical gamepads never raise the mask (the touch overlay is hidden in
     controller mode), so a real right stick still drives Free Look.
     `cvar gSohIos.TouchCMask 0` is the A/B switch.

  3. z_camera.c (Camera_Free) -- INSTRUMENTATION ONLY: publish play->camX/camY
     and a Camera_Free tick count for the console bridge's `look` command, and
     when this tick's touch delta was actually applied (not while shielding,
     same gate as the mouse), a rate-limited log line from the shell proving
     the delta reached the camera.


--- a/soh/soh/Enhancements/controls/Mouse.cpp
+++ b/soh/soh/Enhancements/controls/Mouse.cpp
@@ -16,6 +16,15 @@
 static Ship::Coords mouseCoord = {};
 static Ship::Coords mouseCoordRel = {};
 
+#ifdef __IOS__
+// SOH_IOS (overlay 0062, D-081): touch drag-look. The shell accumulates finger
+// travel (binary-angle units, mouse sign convention) on the main thread; it is
+// drained once per pad tick below and applied like a mouse delta.
+extern "C" void SohIos_TouchLookDrain(float* x, float* y);
+static f32 sSohIosTouchLookX = 0.0f;
+static f32 sSohIosTouchLookY = 0.0f;
+#endif
+
 #define CVAR_ENABLE_MOUSE_NAME CVAR_SETTING("EnableMouse")
 #define CVAR_ENABLE_MOUSE_DEFAULT 0
 #define CVAR_ENABLE_MOUSE_VALUE CVarGetInteger(CVAR_ENABLE_MOUSE_NAME, CVAR_ENABLE_MOUSE_DEFAULT)
@@ -32,8 +41,19 @@
 
 void Mouse_UpdatePosRel() {
     mouseCoordRel = GetWindow()->GetMouseDelta();
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    SohIos_TouchLookDrain(&sSohIosTouchLookX, &sSohIosTouchLookY);
+#endif
 }
 
+#ifdef __IOS__
+// This tick's touch drag-look delta (overlay 0062): Camera_Free's log line.
+void Mouse_SohIosTouchLookTick(f32* x, f32* y) {
+    *x = sSohIosTouchLookX;
+    *y = sSohIosTouchLookY;
+}
+#endif
+
 void Mouse_UpdateAll() {
     Mouse_UpdatePos();
     Mouse_UpdatePosRel();
@@ -44,6 +64,10 @@
         *newCamX -= mouseCoordRel.x * 40.0f;
         *newCamY -= mouseCoordRel.y * 40.0f;
     }
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    *newCamX -= sSohIosTouchLookX;
+    *newCamY -= sSohIosTouchLookY;
+#endif
 }
 
 void Mouse_HandleFirstPerson(Player* player) {
--- a/soh/src/code/padmgr.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/padmgr.c
@@ -227,6 +227,20 @@
         switch (padnow1->err_no) {
             case 0:
                 input->cur = *padnow1;
+
+#ifdef __IOS__
+                /* SOH_IOS (overlay 0062, D-081): touch C-buttons reach the C bits
+                 * through SDL RIGHTX/RIGHTY, which LUS ALSO maps to the N64 right
+                 * stick -- Free Look's camera rate. While a touch C is down (and
+                 * 0.25 s after), port 1's right stick is not the player's. */
+                {
+                    extern int SohIos_TouchCMaskActive(void);
+                    if (i == 0 && SohIos_TouchCMaskActive()) {
+                        input->cur.right_stick_x = 0;
+                        input->cur.right_stick_y = 0;
+                    }
+                }
+#endif
 
                 if (GameInteractor_DisableZTargetingActive()) {
                     input->cur.button &= ~(BTN_Z);
--- a/soh/src/code/z_camera.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_camera.c
@@ -1530,6 +1530,25 @@
         camera->play->camY = -0x228C;
     }
 
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    /* SOH_IOS (overlay 0062, D-081): drag-look instruments (console `look`). */
+    {
+        extern volatile int gSohIosFreeCamX;
